## User-requested bug
Recipient grant issue/list/revoke exists, but ordinary relay dm send and connector outbound still use /send and cannot consume a contact grant. A registered peer with a valid route cannot use the normal send workflow against private reachability; NAS DM smoke returned contact_unauthorised.

## Existing partial fix — inspect before duplicating
Unmerged branch fix/contact-deliver-client, commit 3513ca6c244a9c777143735bbb577504018f6a58, worktree ~/src/c2c/.worktrees/contact-deliver-client.
Adds explicit relay contact deliver with private grant JSON, stable message-id, signed /contact/v1/deliver and HTTPS enforcement. Built/tested in isolation; NOT installed or NAS-tested. Reported TLS integration covers success, duplicates, wrong sender, HTTP refusal, file permissions, revocation and signed inbox polling. Parent verified commit and command help only. Generic sends/tools/connectors remain grant-unaware.

## Acceptance
- Review/reuse partial fix, avoid duplicate overlapping CLI work; follow repo exact-source/buildbox gates before install.
- Provide supported protected grant import/storage/selection/sharing/rotation/revocation UX; no secrets on argv/logs or metadata/list outputs.
- Ordinary CLI sends, connector persisted outbox/retries and supported agent tool/plugin paths select intended grant and use contact admission, with correct sender/recipient identity, destination and reply route. Separate reverse grant for replies.
- No fallback to legacy /send on missing/invalid/expired/revoked grant. Clear actionable diagnostics without recipient enumeration or secret leakage.
- Stable message IDs and crash/restart/response-loss tests prove exactly-once effects and pending-mail preservation. Mixed-version compatibility and explicit LAN transport opt-in integrate without weakening defaults.
- Test two actual hosts in both directions with reply, denied sender, revoke/rotate, restart and duplicates; publish source/binary/hash receipts. A room message is not a DM proof.
- Keep machine-wide public relay settings, connector lease keys and foreign registrations intact.

## Related but distinct
P9 T3 uses shared send/connector code: coordinate one serial integration lane; this generic client bug must not silently rewrite/close P9.M2.E1.T003 or substitute NAS tests for its public-relay proof.
Hermes fixed-target delivery/wake is separately scoped by I016; no claim that grant CLI alone wires an existing live TUI session.
Deployment docs: lan-swarm operations/c2c-relay-dev-nas.md.

Execution decision (2026-10-22): user explicitly authorized implementation. Reuse draft 3513ca6c in a dedicated integration worktree; B369 transport policy lands first in the same serial lane, then shared grant storage/selection, normal CLI/connector/agent surfaces and two-host proof. New sources invalidate prior exact-source/install receipts. Public P9 proof remains separate; T004 review waits for T003.